│ attending a skin clinic in Tehran, Iran. The impact of age, gender, duration of disease, education, extent of        │
│ disease and family history of AA were also assessed. RESULTS Eighty patients (38 male and 42 female) with a mean age │
│ of 27.5 years (SD = 9.3) and disease duration of 7.8 years (SD = 7.7) completed the questionnaire. 76.9% of the      │
│ patients believed that the role of stress was the cause of disease. 17.1 % believed genetic background to be the     │
│ main cause, this found to be more frequent in patients with positive family history of AA. More than half of         │
│ patients believed that their illness had major consequences on their lives and 40% of patients believed that their   │
│ illness would be likely to be permanent rather than temporary, more in patients with longer duration of disease.     │
│ Only 57.5% of patients considered their treatments to be effective. CONCLUSION AA may considerably affect various    │
